# Saltmirror Array: mostly flat-out on the salt, broken by two banks and a
# run through the fynbos range. Units in metres: x east, z south.
#
# East down the array's arm, 600 m between the dish pedestals with a pad
# every 120 m; round the inside wall of a dish that fell off its mount, a
# bowl banked at 45 degrees; out over its rim past the first cactus knoll
# (a kart that kept its boosts and takes the pad high on the wall flies
# straight over the knoll); a slalom round the other two; north into the
# fynbos over blind crests and up onto the old shoreline, where a long
# sweeper round a spur is the second bank; down off the benches through the
# gypsum dunes and across the brine flat, slick as ice, to the line.
track saltmirror_array size 1024 style saltpan
title SALTMIRROR ARRAY
blurb A late-summer evening on a salt pan under eleven abandoned radio dishes: a pad-chained straight down the array, a fallen dish ridden as a 45-degree bowl, a slalom round the cactus knolls, a climb through the fynbos to the old shoreline, and the brine flat home.
race laps 2 rivals 5 vehicle kart
road 18 bank 1.2
land 30 0.6
hour 18
materials verge salt_plates

# The range in the north: the old shorelines as benches, 12 and 26 m over
# the pan, and a spur the upper one goes round.
